Z||000000||sqoach||04-24-2001||08:44 PM||||Ok, so maybe it's not part 34, but who knows. Anyway, I got a question. Should I see bubbles in my overflow tank when my car is running?<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||04-24-2001||09:37 PM||||NO!<BR>You have a cracked block, blown head gasket, or other problem that allows combustion gasses into the cooling system...<BR>BIG job ahead, perhaps you should give it to me for a parts car...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||04-24-2001||09:40 PM||||It's sounding more and more like the head gasket or a crack.  Hope against all hope that it is a head gasket, still a lot of work but not as much as buying a new head or swapping in a new engine!<P>------------------<BR>AIM: FieroJoe87<BR>87 Coupe 5spd<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||04-24-2001||09:52 PM||||Ok, if it was the head gasket or a crack somewhere, what else would tell me this? I think the reason I saw bubbles was because I already had some air in the water system. They weren't little bitty bubbles that just flowed out. It was just a few every now and then. They were about pea-sized (little peas)||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||04-24-2001||11:25 PM||||Actually the answer depends.....<P>If you just filled it... then the cooling system is going to work some air out for awhile. It's suposed to do that. That's one of the recovery tank functions. air goes out when it heat up but only coolant gets pulled in when it cools.<P><BR>One thing to do is pull the thermostat and lock the rad fan on. AC clutch should be disabled. (I think a fuse will do that or unplug the clutch. I'm not looking it up now.) If you don't want to mess with AC use the fan switch on the block.<P>leave the cap off the thermo neck and start it. If you see bubbles here more than a few seconds then you've likely got a head gasket problem. Again if you just filled you'll get some air, but it should clear out quickly from here. Bubbles still flowing after a couple minutes would be bad.<P>You did check to make sure you have the NON vented rad cap? I forgot if you did.... they are explained in my cave. That cap is important.<P>Another symptom of a head is the cooling system reaching full pressure before the coolant is actually hot.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fiero_Freak||04-24-2001||11:40 PM||||   Ditto on the filler neck check.  You might have your radiator cap pressure tested, or hell splurg the $5 and buy another. <BR>   If not how do you feel about the 3.4L upgrade?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero_Left_01.jpg"> <BR>Two '87 GT's...<BR>   ...Double Trouble||||reg||1
Z||000006||sqoach||04-25-2001||01:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<BR><B>Another symptom of a head is the cooling system reaching full pressure before the coolant is actually hot.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think this is the problem. It's never actually really hot. It does get pretty warm though. Seems like an abundance of pressure is building up when it's not suppose to. And I got the right cap. A 16lb non-vented one.<P>Oh yeah, if I leave the cap off of the stat housing, won't the coolant run over? It seems like I did that before, and that's what happened.<P>Fiero_Freak, a 3.4 upgrade (or any upgrade) is out of the question for me. My piggy bank only has about $60  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||04-25-2001||07:24 PM||||what motor is it???<P>You should be able to start it with the stat out of the neck and see what it's doing... <P>You might cough out some water but most should stay in. You want to do this cold.... If you are blowing allot of coolant then the question becomes did you check all the plumbing for blockage/damage?||||reg||1
Z||000008||sqoach||04-25-2001||11:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<BR><B>what motor is it???<P>You should be able to start it with the stat out of the neck and see what it's doing... <P>You might cough out some water but most should stay in. You want to do this cold.... If you are blowing allot of coolant then the question becomes did you check all the plumbing for blockage/damage?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>86 2.5L<P>Um...I haven't taken all the hoses out and inspected them, if that's what you mean. I'm deciding if I want to do that or not. It seems to be flowing fine, but I'm not completely sure. I guess I'll have to take a day and check all of the hoses.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||theogre||04-26-2001||07:29 PM||||AS long as you start cold... you should be able to run the 4 cyl with the stat out and cover off. If you spit up more than a cup or 2 of water I'd start looking for a blockage. The head gasket won't usually make it spit up unless it's totally fried. You'll just see the afore mentioned bubbles flowing.<P>If there's no pinched hose or hard line then pulling the hoses off may be the next option. Someone may have droped something in it...||||reg||1
Z||000010||84Bill||04-26-2001||11:38 PM||||Hey sqoach<BR> I just got done pulling off those pipes and I did not find all the much grunge in there however I did have a nice kink in the tube near the rear of the car. It was almost pinched closed ! apparently someone had bent it back down but due to the small dia of the pipe it looked normal but viewed from the side it was not a pretty sight. Just thaugt I'd let you know......||||reg||11
Z||000011||sqoach||04-27-2001||12:49 PM||||84Bill, how long did it take to pull all the hoses and pipes? Any certain ones that were a pain in the a$$? I'm going to have to wait until next week cuz my weekend is full.||||reg||1
Z||000012||84Bill||04-27-2001||01:03 PM||||Nah wasn't all the dificult just the hoses front and rear and the 3 brackets along the sides and front. Infact I didnt even have to jack up the car to get to anything. took about 15 minutes or so TT. <BR>Tools reqd <BR>1 10 million meter sockett <BR>1 flat screwdriver<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 04-27-2001).]||||reg||1
